To ensure robust evaluation and account for potential stochasticity in LLM outputs, we set $n=100$ , evaluating each summary $100$ times across both closed and open-source LLMs. A temperature of 0.0 was used to ensure deterministic outputs, aiming for consistent, high-quality results crucial for reproducibility and reliable evaluation.

