We distinguish three types of hits in a given phase:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item Hits under both policies. We denote the set of accesses that hit under both policies in phase $i$ as $\hitsBoth{i}$.
	\item Hits under $\lru(l)$ but not under $\mru(k)$, which we denote by $\hitsLRU{i}$.
	\item Hits under $\mru(k)$ but not under $\lru(l)$, which we denote by $\hitsNMRU{i}$.
\end{enumerate}
This is illustrated by the following Venn diagram:
