%theorems of cooperative game theory states that a TU-game has a non-empty
%core if and only if it is balanced.



The result presented by \cite{bondareva1963some} and \cite{shapley1967balanced} provides a necessary and sufficient condition for the non-emptiness of the core of a TU-game. Specifically, one of the key theorems in cooperative game theory asserts that a TU-game has a non-empty core if and only if it is balanced.

