			Consider the electrostatic potential generated by unit point charges at the vertices of a triangular or square anti-prism. Then, for relative heights smaller than $\sqrt{2}$, there is an equilibrium on any of the segments connecting the center of the anti-prism to the midpoints of every lateral edge.
