	We now return to the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}. By Claims~\ref{tree1}-\ref{tree28}, we conclude that $T$ does not contains any tree $T_i$ shown in Figure~\ref{trees} as a subtree for $i\in [28]$, a contradiction to Claim~\ref{cl-2}. We deduce, therefore, that our supposition that Theorem~\ref{thm:main} is false is incorrect. Hence every maximal outerplanar of order $n \ge 7$ with $k$ vertices of degree~$2$ satisfies $\gamma_2^d(G) \le  \floor*{\frac{2}{9}(n+k)}$. This completes the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}.	
