\textbf{Strip-Mining-Free Vector Extension:} To address the fixed register count and power-of-two register group issues found in RVV, a flexible RISC-V vector instruction extension without strip-mining is proposed. 
%It allows scalable configurations for both the number and length of vector registers. Moreover, leveraging the surplus of physical registers, the extension incorporates register-level gather and scatter instructions to minimize the need for memory-level data rearrangement.

\textbf{Arbitrary Register Grouping Strategy:} A register allocation strategy that adapts dynamically to the circumstances is introduced, intelligently modulating the distribution of registers in accordance with real-time vector lengths and the current register availability. 
%This approach abandons the rigidly fixed grouping methods, precisely aligning the number of registers with the data requirements. As a result, it minimizes both superfluous register usage and the movement of data.

\textbf{Compilation Support:} Intrinsic splitting and assembly coalescing passes have been developed, together with a comprehensive compilation mechanism for Zoozve using LLVM, allowing effortless conversion from high-level code to efficient machine instructions. 
