\section{Quantitative Method}
\textbf{Creating the Field Demographics Categories}\\
\label{appendix:creating-field}
We collected the research fields that our participants studied in the form of free responses. Out of the 816 responses, 644 (79\%) responses included field information. We classified 635 free responses into four field categories: computer science, social science \& humanities, natural science \& engineering, and biology \& medicine, and 9 responses were classified as other and excluded from the analysis. Computer science group had 257 participants, and also included interdisciplinary fields with computer science, such as education technology, except biotechnology. Social science \& humanities had 152 participants, and included psychology, behavioral science, education, sociology, and more. Natural science \& engineering had 132 participants, and included math, chemistry, physics, environmental science, electrical engineering, and more. Biology \& medicine had 94 responses, and included cognitive science, bioinformatics, biotechnology, public health, neuroscience, and more.


