Secondly, let us discuss cSGD-iVI method.
For calculating the gradient term in each iteration step, we need to solve one adjoint PDE (corresponding to computing $H^{*}$), and one forward PDE (corresponding to computing $H$).
Then each iteration we need to calculate $2$ PDEs.
%For calculating the eigenvalues \( \{ a_i, \phi_i \}^M_{i = 1} \) in each iteration step, we need to calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of $H^*H$ for accuracy based on \cite{bui2013computational}, and we can neglected when eigenvalues are smaller than $1$.
